    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The three test files are `AcceptanceTest` (the only one with `@Test` methods), plus the `AcceptanceBase` base class and `AuditLogCapture` helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented disposable-domain email blocking that rejects owner creation with HTTP 400, following the repository's existing custom-validation pattern (`TelephoneValidation`/`AddressValidation`):\n\n1. **`EmailDomainValidation.java`** \u2014 a new Bean Validation constraint annotation (field-level, runtime-retained), mirroring the existing validation annotations.\n\n2. **`EmailDomainValidator.java`** \u2014 the `ConstraintValidator` implementation. It extracts the domain (after the last `@`), lower-cases it, and rejects it if it's one of `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`. `null` and malformed (no `@`) values are deferred to the existing `@Email` constraint, matching how the sibling validators defer to `@NotBlank`/`@Email`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `@EmailDomainValidation` alongside the existing `@Email` annotation on the `OwnerFields.email` field, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` carries the constraint and Bean Validation produces a 400 on the `POST /api/owners` endpoint.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) now returns 400, and the full build passes.",
